   "preinstalled": {
    "zh": "编排镜像：上游代码（固定提交、未改）、uv 锁定依赖、docker CLI（经 shim 给兄弟容器加代理和 CA）；agent 镜像：上游自己的 agent-cli Dockerfile",
    "en": "orchestrator image: upstream code at the pin (unmodified), uv-locked dependencies, the docker CLI (a shim adds proxy and CA to sibling containers); agent image: upstream's own agent-cli Dockerfile"
   }
  },
  "roles": [],
  "world": null,
  "notes": {
   "benchmark_paths": "A benchmark item's paths are mounted into the agent containers unless upstream mounts the same path itself (/workspace and below, /home/agent-home, /task-source, /run, /tmp): those are left out and listed in logs/sibling-mounts.txt. The agents work in upstream's own /workspace (the run directory), so a deliverable the official prompt names under such a path is not written where the run collects it.",
   "venue": "paper.paper_format=iclr for every task. The system has only iclr and alife specs and does not choose a venue itself; ICML and NeurIPS templates and a system-chosen venue are unsupported.",
   "task_input": "Only the `# Goal` and `# Rubrics` sections of task.md are read: all five candidate files are put under `# Goal` with their headings turned into bold lines; `# Rubrics` carries a neutral line. The paradigm is optimisation of a scalar score: the task-drafting phase (documented as experimental) turns the brief into an evaluator and a seed program.",
   "phases": "execution.phases=task_drafting,investigation,final_evaluation,paper; the system's own default also runs ablations and posthoc; final_evaluation stays because a drafted task requires it before the paper. review/revision (second model) are never selected.",
   "agent_pool": "agent.pool and agent.models.* are left empty: one model for every phase.",
   "second_provider": "No OPENAI/GEMINI key is supplied (concept figures stay in deterministic export mode): the Codex placeholder is not named OPENAI_API_KEY for that reason.",
   "time": "No global wall-clock or token cap exists upstream; the runner enforces time_limit_hours. Native caps used: idea cycles=3, per-phase timeouts from [systems.agentic-scientist].",
   "network": "Sibling agent containers run on the shield's internal network; the agents keep their CLI WebFetch/Bash network, which go through the shield. Provider hosts are only tunnelled by the shield.",
   "search": "Provider server-side web search is switched off in every sibling by the agent CLIs' own system settings, bind-mounted read-only by the docker shim: Claude Code /etc/claude-code/managed-settings.json (permissions.deny WebSearch), Codex /etc/codex/config.toml (web_search=\"disabled\") and /etc/codex/requirements.toml (allowed_web_search_modes=[\"disabled\"]). Upstream's own Semantic Scholar client goes through the shield.",
   "key_exposure": "none: the siblings hold only a placeholder in RWE_CODEX_API_KEY (set by the docker shim, not in upstream's env file); the shield proxy puts codex-api's local key on the request and the login stays on the host",
   "gpu": "gpus=1 is wired (container.gpu_count, harness GPU evaluation) but was not exercised.",
   "docker_socket": "The orchestrator has its run's private docker socket; the privileged daemon is root-equivalent.",
   "model_access": "the project's own ChatGPT (Codex) login through codex-api  (account codex-jacques): the siblings' Codex CLI gets a custom provider (rwe_codex_api, Responses API) in /etc/codex/config.toml, at the one host address the shield lets through; the model and the effort come from upstream's own switches (agent.model, agent.reasoning_effort -> `codex exec --model`, `-c model_reasoning_effort`)",
   "empty_closing_message": "Sol sometimes ends a turn with an empty closing message; upstream's agent launcher (Headless) then exits 1 with 'headless: could not extract final message; rerun with --json for raw trace' and upstream ends the phase. A wrapper (headless-compat.sh, in place of the launcher in the siblings' command) runs the real launcher unchanged and turns exactly that one exit, with that line as its whole stderr, into 0; any other error stays. What the step produced is still checked by upstream. The usage line the launcher would have printed for that turn is not printed."
  },
